1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,746
A slow ball just taps your pads.

2
00:00:02,746 --> 00:00:04,202
A fast ball stings.

3
00:00:04,202 --> 00:00:06,913
A hammer swung hard drives a nail deep.

4
00:00:07,313 --> 00:00:09,119
Moving things carry something.

5
00:00:09,119 --> 00:00:11,587
Something that can push, hit and break.

6
00:00:12,037 --> 00:00:13,953
Aarav is at the college nets.

7
00:00:13,953 --> 00:00:16,398
A ball comes at ten metres per second.

8
00:00:16,398 --> 00:00:18,034
Just a tap on the pads.

9
00:00:18,384 --> 00:00:20,295
The next ball comes at twenty.

10
00:00:20,295 --> 00:00:21,409
Twice the speed.

11
00:00:21,409 --> 00:00:23,139
Does it hit twice as hard?

12
00:00:23,639 --> 00:00:24,539
No.

13
00:00:24,042 --> 00:00:26,025
It carries four times the energy.

14
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,744
By the end of this
video, you will see why.

15
00:00:29,394 --> 00:00:31,163
So what is kinetic energy?

16
00:00:31,513 --> 00:00:32,579
First, energy.

17
00:00:32,579 --> 00:00:36,844
Energy is the ability to do work: to
push something through a distance.

18
00:00:37,244 --> 00:00:39,532
A moving hammer pushes a nail in.

19
00:00:39,532 --> 00:00:41,918
A moving ball pushes the pads back.

20
00:00:41,918 --> 00:00:43,841
Moving air turns a windmill.

21
00:00:44,241 --> 00:00:46,967
Each one does work, just
because it is moving.

22
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:51,776
The energy a body has because of
its motion is called kinetic energy.

23
00:00:51,776 --> 00:00:54,610
Kinetic comes from a
Greek word for motion.

24
00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:55,880
Its symbol is K.

25
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:58,436
Let's build it on a live track.

26
00:00:58,786 --> 00:01:01,202
A two kilogram cart starts at rest.

27
00:01:01,202 --> 00:01:04,896
A steady four newton force
pushes it, with no friction.

28
00:01:05,296 --> 00:01:08,676
After one metre, it moves
at two metres per second.

29
00:01:08,676 --> 00:01:11,264
The force has done four joules of work.

30
00:01:11,664 --> 00:01:14,296
After four metres, the speed is four.

31
00:01:14,296 --> 00:01:16,206
The work is sixteen joules.

32
00:01:16,606 --> 00:01:19,234
After nine metres, the speed is six.

33
00:01:19,234 --> 00:01:20,594
Thirty six joules.

34
00:01:20,994 --> 00:01:23,721
Slow-mo replay of the first four metres.

35
00:01:24,071 --> 00:01:28,826
To double the speed, the same push had
to act over four times the distance.

36
00:01:28,826 --> 00:01:30,936
So four times the work went in.

37
00:01:31,536 --> 00:01:32,871
Look at the graph.

38
00:01:32,871 --> 00:01:35,340
The stored work is the kinetic energy.

39
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:37,414
It curves up, like v squared.

40
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:40,472
Now the formula, one step at a time.

41
00:01:40,822 --> 00:01:41,722
Step one.

42
00:01:41,649 --> 00:01:45,398
A force F pushes a body from
rest through a distance d.

43
00:01:45,398 --> 00:01:47,646
The work done is W equals F d.

44
00:01:48,396 --> 00:01:49,296
Step two.

45
00:01:49,247 --> 00:01:50,679
Newton's second law.

46
00:01:50,679 --> 00:01:51,863
F equals m a.

47
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:53,520
Step three.

48
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:56,618
Starting from rest, v
squared equals two a d.

49
00:01:56,618 --> 00:01:58,966
So d equals v squared over two a.

50
00:01:59,716 --> 00:02:00,670
Step four.

51
00:02:00,670 --> 00:02:02,128
Put them together.

52
00:02:02,128 --> 00:02:05,418
W equals m a, times v squared over two a.

53
00:02:05,418 --> 00:02:06,658
The a cancels.

54
00:02:06,658 --> 00:02:08,752
W equals half m v squared.

55
00:02:09,502 --> 00:02:10,413
Step five.

56
00:02:10,413 --> 00:02:12,895
This work is stored in the motion.

57
00:02:12,895 --> 00:02:16,832
So kinetic energy K equals
half m v squared, in joules.

58
00:02:17,582 --> 00:02:18,482
Step six.

59
00:02:18,438 --> 00:02:20,160
Momentum p equals m v.

60
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:23,730
So K can also be written
as p squared over two m.

61
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:25,524
Remember this.

62
00:02:25,524 --> 00:02:27,885
Kinetic energy is half m v squared.

63
00:02:27,885 --> 00:02:31,349
Double the speed, and you
get four times the energy.

64
00:02:32,049 --> 00:02:33,707
Now, mass or speed?

65
00:02:33,707 --> 00:02:34,870
Side by side.

66
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,148
Double the mass, same speed.

67
00:02:37,148 --> 00:02:38,048
K doubles.

68
00:02:37,967 --> 00:02:39,603
Four joules become eight.

69
00:02:40,003 --> 00:02:42,093
Double the speed, same mass.

70
00:02:42,093 --> 00:02:43,662
K becomes four times.

71
00:02:43,662 --> 00:02:45,537
Four joules become sixteen.

72
00:02:46,137 --> 00:02:47,211
Now you try.

73
00:02:47,211 --> 00:02:51,716
One kilogram at six metres per
second, or two kilograms at three.

74
00:02:51,716 --> 00:02:53,854
Which has more kinetic energy?

75
00:02:53,854 --> 00:02:55,188
Pause and decide.

76
00:02:58,388 --> 00:02:59,907
The light, fast ball!

77
00:02:59,907 --> 00:03:03,463
Eighteen joules against nine,
because the speed is squared.

78
00:03:04,113 --> 00:03:06,522
Can kinetic energy ever be negative?

79
00:03:06,522 --> 00:03:07,802
Follow the links.

80
00:03:08,152 --> 00:03:09,052
One.

81
00:03:08,623 --> 00:03:10,184
Mass is always positive.

82
00:03:10,584 --> 00:03:11,484
Two.

83
00:03:11,093 --> 00:03:14,935
v squared is never negative,
whichever way the body moves.

84
00:03:15,335 --> 00:03:16,235
Three.

85
00:03:15,983 --> 00:03:17,787
So K is never negative.

86
00:03:17,787 --> 00:03:19,368
It has no direction.

87
00:03:19,368 --> 00:03:20,684
It is a scalar.

88
00:03:21,084 --> 00:03:21,984
One more.

89
00:03:21,869 --> 00:03:26,208
A ball's velocity flips from plus
four to minus four metres per second.

90
00:03:26,208 --> 00:03:28,219
Does its kinetic energy change?

91
00:03:28,219 --> 00:03:29,397
Pause and think.

92
00:03:32,597 --> 00:03:33,497
No!

93
00:03:33,013 --> 00:03:34,599
The speed is still four.

94
00:03:34,599 --> 00:03:38,222
Its momentum flipped, but its
kinetic energy stayed the same.

95
00:03:38,872 --> 00:03:40,562
Now, one worked example.

96
00:03:40,912 --> 00:03:45,284
A cricket ball of zero point one six
kilograms is bowled at twenty metres

97
00:03:45,284 --> 00:03:46,184
per second.

98
00:03:46,171 --> 00:03:50,890
Find its kinetic energy, and the speed
at which it has a quarter of that.

99
00:03:51,390 --> 00:03:53,363
K equals half m v squared.

100
00:03:53,363 --> 00:03:57,124
Half, times zero point one
six, times twenty squared.

101
00:03:57,874 --> 00:03:59,969
Twenty squared is four hundred.

102
00:03:59,969 --> 00:04:03,969
Zero point zero eight times four
hundred is thirty two joules.

103
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:07,449
A quarter of thirty two is eight joules.

104
00:04:07,449 --> 00:04:11,589
K is a quarter, so v squared
is a quarter, and v is half.

105
00:04:12,339 --> 00:04:13,819
Ten metres per second.

106
00:04:13,819 --> 00:04:17,551
Aarav's slow ball: half the
speed, a quarter of the energy.

107
00:04:18,201 --> 00:04:19,663
Now, the exam trap.

108
00:04:20,013 --> 00:04:23,720
Many students think two bodies with
the same momentum have the same kinetic

109
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,620
energy.

110
00:04:24,604 --> 00:04:26,944
But K equals p squared over two m.

111
00:04:26,944 --> 00:04:30,999
For the same momentum, the lighter
body has more kinetic energy.

112
00:04:31,649 --> 00:04:33,069
Where is this asked?

113
00:04:33,069 --> 00:04:37,805
In quick ratio and percentage questions
linking K, mass, speed and momentum.

114
00:04:38,405 --> 00:04:39,588
Exam level now.

115
00:04:39,588 --> 00:04:43,959
A trolley's momentum increases by
fifty percent, with the same mass.

116
00:04:43,959 --> 00:04:47,298
By what percentage does its
kinetic energy increase?

117
00:04:47,298 --> 00:04:48,531
Pause and solve.

118
00:04:53,931 --> 00:04:55,321
The answer is B.

119
00:04:55,321 --> 00:04:57,919
One hundred and twenty five percent.

120
00:04:58,419 --> 00:05:00,620
K equals p squared over two m.

121
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:03,491
With the same mass, K follows p squared.

122
00:05:03,991 --> 00:05:09,022
The new p is one point five p, so
the new K is two point two five times

123
00:05:09,022 --> 00:05:09,922
K.

124
00:05:09,953 --> 00:05:12,643
The increase is one point two five K.

125
00:05:12,643 --> 00:05:15,156
One hundred and twenty five percent.

126
00:05:15,756 --> 00:05:17,292
Here is your recap.

127
00:05:17,292 --> 00:05:18,871
Screenshot this card.

128
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:24,257
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

129
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:25,557
One.

130
00:05:25,115 --> 00:05:28,868
Why does a ball at twice the
speed carry four times the energy?

131
00:05:29,768 --> 00:05:30,668
Two.

132
00:05:30,254 --> 00:05:32,555
Can kinetic energy ever be negative?

133
00:05:33,455 --> 00:05:34,355
Three.

134
00:05:34,004 --> 00:05:36,084
Two bodies have the same momentum.

135
00:05:36,084 --> 00:05:38,164
Which one has more kinetic energy?

136
00:05:39,264 --> 00:05:43,498
Next time: a bike going twice as
fast needs four times the distance to

137
00:05:43,498 --> 00:05:44,398
stop.

138
00:05:44,026 --> 00:05:44,926
Why?

139
00:05:44,507 --> 00:05:46,931
We find out in the work-energy theorem.
